From e006f1132339e5fe8a36e5216c8112b2611080f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 02:01:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ci: path-gate the Windows matrix, add an aggregate gate, fix
 the local test lane

Measured 2026-08-16: Windows Full Matrix median 11.5 min vs 2.2 min on ubuntu
(5.2x) and it ran on 100% of 25 sampled PR runs. Pipeline wall median 12.3 min.

- test.yml: new `changes` job classifies the PR diff; `full-matrix` now runs only
  when OS-sensitive paths change. Every non-pull_request event (push to master,
  the new merge_group trigger, schedule, workflow_dispatch) still runs the full
  3-OS x 2-Node matrix unconditionally, and an unresolvable diff fails safe to it.
  Cross-OS signal on a skipped PR still comes from Windows Smoke, macOS Smoke and
  the windows-node22 Targeted PR Tests lane.
- test.yml: new `CI Gate` job aggregates every real lane with `if: always()`,
  passing on success-or-skipped and failing on any failure/cancellation. Intended
  to replace `Cross-OS Gate` as the single required context (branch protection is
  NOT changed here).
- required-checks-bypass.yml: matching `CI Gate` no-op, and paths-ignore aligned
  with test.yml's paths so the two workflows can no longer both post a check.
- concurrency + cancel-in-progress on the PR-triggered workflows that lacked it
  (pr-monitor keeps its documented opt-out).
- timeout-minutes on every job in every hand-maintained workflow.
- Local test lane: bun.lock was never targetable (the list only knew the older
  bun.lockb), and validation/, eval/, rules/, plugin/, lefthook.yml,
  eslint.config.js and the plugin marketplace manifest resolved zero tests. All
  now map to their real suites. Measured over the last 300 commits on master this
  drops the full-suite fallback rate from 19.0% to 12.3%.
- test/QUARANTINE.md plus the AGENTS.md rule: flaky tests get quarantined and an
  issue filed, never retried until green. No auto-retry mechanism is introduced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
